   "title": "PHerc0139 secondary set: distance from the predicted sheet to the wrap segment",
   "caption": "Secondary set (PHerc0139, PREREG 4.10): distance |d| from the predicted sheet to the matched wrap segment, in sv (1 sv = 9.596 µm); 36 scored fibers, 283 of 284 planned stretches scored (the report lists 1 skips). (a) The report holds no per-node distances, only these points of the pooled per-node distribution: the median and p90 (horizontal bars: fiber-bootstrap 95 % CI) and the fractions within 1 and 2 sv (vertical bars: CI); marks of different surfaces (point or CI bar) that would overlap are moved apart, perpendicular to the value they show, here by at most 0.007 up or down (median, p90) and 0.06 sv sideways (within 1 and 2 sv); every other mark is at its value. Strip: all scored nodes; frame plane and Lasagna plane: the nodes covered by both the strip and that baseline; fiber floor: the human fiber itself, one point per scored row (its count is of rows; no CI in the report). Below: pooled mean |d| with its CI. Strip: mean 1.20 sv [1.05, 1.46], median 0.80 sv, p90 2.54 sv, within 2 sv 84.1 % [78.4, 87.4] %; frame plane 2.92 sv [2.63, 3.14]; Lasagna plane 3.15 sv [2.46, 3.79]; fiber floor 0.88 sv. G2 (PREREG 6) needs a pooled mean ≤ 1.5 sv, at least 70 % of nodes within 2 sv and both baselines beaten; the report's verdict: “secondary: transfers”. (b) Per fiber: the cumulative fraction of scored fibers by their mean |d| over each surface's own covered nodes (node-weighted over the fiber's strips, from per_strip; a baseline only for fibers with at least 25 of its nodes); the dotted line is the fiber floor's pooled mean.",
